: "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the failing test and the money module.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012Y94WCDxoe3cFAzS1eMqNP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ENWA398ZoZmvfbXn6r75Sg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011pcfbAeAPtaqZZgTad39vu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Both test cases match half-even: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 (the 7 is odd, so it rounds up to the even 8) and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 (the 6 is already even). I'll create a branch and make the fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NPBnC6QzZRKvenmWvmtFT8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PoZRAu1GxHPAUPvtaDhkef", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01848RbrB5t87bSVeNxG